From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:35:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: Scale the escan timeout with the channel
 count

The escan timer allows a flat 10 seconds, but the firmware dwells up to
BRCMF_SCAN_PASSIVE_TIME on each channel it may only listen on. The
BCM4388 has 100 channels, and all 60 of its 6 GHz channels are passive:
on the J713 a passive scan of all of them takes 14.9 seconds, and iwd's
scans of 5 and 6 GHz while disconnected took 10.7, so the timer aborted
them and the station could not find its network.

Allow 2 seconds plus 280 ms per channel, twice the passive dwell and a
channel switch: 30 seconds for all 100 channels, 2.3 seconds for one.
P2P scans, which dwell up to 200 ms, fit within it too.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
---
 .../wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c  | 12 +++++++++++-
 .../wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.h  |  1 -
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
index 029d2407f184..bd97021c8aa9 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
@@ -85,6 +85,14 @@
 #define BRCMF_SCAN_UNASSOC_TIME		40
 #define BRCMF_SCAN_PASSIVE_TIME		120
 
+/*
+ * E-Scan timeout. Per channel, the firmware dwells for up to
+ * BRCMF_SCAN_PASSIVE_TIME (P2P scans up to 200 ms) and, while associated,
+ * also returns to its own channel; allow twice the passive dwell.
+ */
+#define BRCMF_ESCAN_TIMEOUT_BASE_MS	2000
+#define BRCMF_ESCAN_TIMEOUT_CHANNEL_MS	(2 * BRCMF_SCAN_PASSIVE_TIME + 40)
+
 #define BRCMF_ND_INFO_TIMEOUT		msecs_to_jiffies(2000)
 
 #define BRCMF_PS_MAX_TIMEOUT_MS		2000
@@ -1231,7 +1239,9 @@ brcmf_cfg80211_scan(struct wiphy *wiphy, struct cfg80211_scan_request *request)
 
 	/* Arm scan timeout timer */
 	mod_timer(&cfg->escan_timeout,
-		  jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies(BRCMF_ESCAN_TIMER_INTERVAL_MS));
+		  jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies(BRCMF_ESCAN_TIMEOUT_BASE_MS +
+					     request->n_channels *
+					     BRCMF_ESCAN_TIMEOUT_CHANNEL_MS));
 
 	return 0;
 
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.h b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.h
index 7cb42b61c83e..92bda966e93e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.h
@@ -47,7 +47,6 @@
  * problematic on some systems and should be avoided.
  */
 #define BRCMF_ESCAN_BUF_SIZE		65000
-#define BRCMF_ESCAN_TIMER_INTERVAL_MS	10000	/* E-Scan timeout */
 
 #define WL_ESCAN_ACTION_START		1
 #define WL_ESCAN_ACTION_CONTINUE	2
